  "narrative": {
    "text": "Fig. 10, 'Product packaging hierarchy' (source: GS1.org), in the section on instituting data management and governance policies. It is drawn as a staircase of four grey steps, each holding packaging illustrations. The top step, labelled PRIMARY, shows individual items such as vials, a bottle, syringes in blister packs, a blister strip and a sterile-packed instrument. The next step, SECONDARY, shows boxes and cartons holding those items; the third, SECONDARY OR TERTIARY, shows open cartons and a row of boxed packs; and the bottom step, TERTIARY, shows shipping cases and a shrink-wrapped pallet of boxes.",
